# KUDIX — GAMING & REWARDS PLATFORM

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
KUDIX is a modern, interactive online gaming platform where users can register, receive gaming credits, play different games, complete social tasks, refer other users, earn referral commissions, access gaming signals, and contact customer support.

The platform should have a professional, premium, modern design that works perfectly on mobile phones, tablets, laptops, and desktops.

### Technology
- HTML
- Tailwind CSS
- JavaScript
- Backend and database integration can be handled separately.

## 2. REGISTRATION AND WELCOME BONUS
When a user successfully registers, the platform automatically credits their account with a ₦20,000 welcome bonus.

IMPORTANT RULES:
- The ₦20,000 is gaming credit for playing games on the KUDIX website.
- The welcome bonus is not withdrawable.
- Users can use the bonus to play eligible games on the platform.
- The welcome bonus must be displayed separately from withdrawable referral commissions or other eligible cash balances.
- The interface must clearly explain the difference between gaming credit and withdrawable funds.
- The system must prevent users from withdrawing the welcome bonus.

## 3. REFERRAL SYSTEM AND GAME ACCESS
Users must refer three eligible users before unlocking access to the games.

Each registered user receives a unique referral link.

The referral dashboard should display:
- Unique referral link
- Copy referral link button
- Number of successful referrals
- Referral progress toward the three-person requirement
- Referral history
- Referral commission balance

Example:

Successful Referrals: 1/3

Referral 1: Completed
Referral 2: Pending
Referral 3: Pending

Once the user meets the referral requirement, the system unlocks access to eligible games.

The referral system must verify registrations and prevent fraudulent or duplicate referrals.

## 4. REFERRAL COMMISSION
Users receive ₦1,000 for each successful, eligible referral.

Example:
- 1 referral = ₦1,000
- 3 referrals = ₦3,000
- 5 referrals = ₦5,000
- 10 referrals = ₦10,000

Referral commissions must be tracked separately from the non-withdrawable welcome bonus.

The admin dashboard must allow the administrator to configure the referral commission and manage eligible referral records.

Any withdrawal functionality must follow clearly published eligibility rules.

## 5. GAMES AVAILABLE ON KUDIX

KUDIX will feature six interactive games.

### Game 1: Colour Prediction
Users select one of four colours:
- Red
- Green
- Black
- Yellow

The game displays the outcome of each round.

### Game 2: Number Prediction
Users select a number from the available options and view the round result.

### Game 3: Heads or Tails
Users predict whether the result will be Heads or Tails.

### Game 4: Up or Down
Users predict whether the outcome will be Up or Down.

### Game 5: Lucky Number
Users select a number and view the result when the round finishes.

### Game 6: Higher or Lower
Users view a playing card and predict whether the next card will have a higher or lower value.

Each game must have:
- A dedicated game interface
- Clear instructions
- Selection controls
- Round status
- Countdown timer when applicable
- Result display
- Recent round history
- Gaming credit balance
- Responsive mobile layout

The games must use consistent design elements while maintaining their individual identities.

## 6. ADMIN DASHBOARD AND GAME MANAGEMENT
The administrator must have a dedicated, secure admin dashboard.

The administrator should be able to:

- View registered users.
- Manage user accounts.
- Enable or disable individual games.
- Configure game settings.
- Configure round durations.
- Manage game rounds.
- Publish official results.
- View round histories.
- Manage promotional gaming credits.
- Configure welcome bonus amounts.
- Configure referral commissions.
- Review referral records.
- Review social task submissions.
- Manage notifications and announcements.
- Manage support conversations.

### Game Results and Signals

The administrator must be able to publish game signals through a dedicated signals section.

Signals may include:
- Game name
- Round identification
- Predicted colour
- Predicted number
- Predicted direction
- Predicted card outcome
- Publication time
- Round status

Users can view published signals through the website's signals page.

Signals must be clearly distinguished from confirmed results. Published predictions must not be presented as guaranteed winning outcomes.

Official game results should be recorded transparently, with appropriate timestamps and round histories.

## 7. SOCIAL TASKS
KUDIX must have a social tasks section where users can complete assigned tasks and upload screenshot proof.

Example tasks:
- Follow an official social media account.
- Join an official community.
- Subscribe to an official channel.
- Share an approved promotional post.

Each task must display:
- Task title
- Instructions
- Reward, if applicable
- Task status
- Screenshot upload field
- Submission button

### Task Submission Process
1. The user opens the Social Tasks page.
2. The user selects an available task.
3. The user follows the instructions.
4. The user uploads a screenshot as proof.
5. The submission is sent to the administrator.
6. The administrator reviews the evidence.
7. The administrator approves or rejects the submission.
8. The user receives a notification of the decision.

### Admin Task Management
The administrator must be able to:
- Create and edit tasks.
- Set task instructions.
- Configure task rewards.
- View uploaded screenshots.
- Approve submissions.
- Reject submissions with a reason.
- Track reviewed submissions.

## 8. CUSTOMER SUPPORT CHATBOT
KUDIX must include a floating customer support chatbot available throughout the website.

When clicked, it opens a modern chat window.

The chatbot should provide options such as:
- Game Access
- Welcome Bonus
- Referral Issues
- Referral Commission
- Social Tasks
- Account Problems
- Speak to a Support Agent

The chatbot should answer common questions and allow users to request assistance from a human support agent.

The support dashboard should allow authorized agents to:
- View support requests.
- Respond to users.
- Review conversation history.
- Manage open and resolved conversations.

## 9. SIGNALS PAGE
Create a dedicated signals page where users can view signals published by the administrator.

Each signal card should display:
- Game name
- Round ID
- Predicted outcome
- Publication timestamp
- Round status
- Final result, when available

The administrator must be able to publish, update, and manage signals through the admin dashboard.

Signals should be clearly labelled as predictions and must not guarantee winnings.

